1
00:00:00,029 --> 00:00:03,599
Unit checklists help vehicle
crews keep each check tied to

2
00:00:03,599 --> 00:00:05,329
the right apparatus and form.

3
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:08,029
Here, Engine 51 is selected.

4
00:00:08,470 --> 00:00:11,369
Open Checklists and look
under Start checklist.

5
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:16,090
Find Engine 51 daily readiness,
then choose the Engine 51

6
00:00:16,090 --> 00:00:17,459
button directly beneath it.

7
00:00:17,940 --> 00:00:22,559
The Ambulance 61 form offers a
same-named target button, so match both

8
00:00:22,559 --> 00:00:24,819
the form and vehicle before starting.

9
00:00:25,030 --> 00:00:27,880
The form opens for Engine 51, Version 1.

10
00:00:28,479 --> 00:00:33,199
Equipment ready for the exercise is the
first item, marked Required and Critical.

11
00:00:33,630 --> 00:00:37,130
Choose Pass for this training run
and add a Note explaining that this

12
00:00:37,130 --> 00:00:40,720
is a software walkthrough and no
physical inspection was performed.

13
00:00:41,119 --> 00:00:44,669
That context makes the simulated
answer clear to the next reader.

14
00:00:45,050 --> 00:00:47,060
Check the note, then choose Next.

15
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:49,569
Stock and supplies recorded is item two.

16
00:00:50,160 --> 00:00:53,370
Choose Pass and add a
supplies-specific note that keeps

17
00:00:53,370 --> 00:00:55,109
the answer within the exercise.

18
00:00:55,439 --> 00:00:59,090
An item note should explain that
particular answer, so the next crew

19
00:00:59,090 --> 00:01:01,149
member can understand what was recorded.

20
00:01:01,609 --> 00:01:04,460
Confirm the heading and
answer, then choose Next.

21
00:01:04,859 --> 00:01:08,589
Use the same review habit for
a patrol kit or SAR cache with

22
00:01:08,589 --> 00:01:09,950
your team's published form.

23
00:01:10,230 --> 00:01:13,050
The third item is Handover notes reviewed.

24
00:01:13,519 --> 00:01:17,770
Choose Pass and record the fictional
handover context in the item's Note.

25
00:01:18,199 --> 00:01:22,000
Below the navigation buttons, the
general note describes the whole run.

26
00:01:22,380 --> 00:01:26,719
Keep its overall training purpose clear;
leave the location field blank here.

27
00:01:27,149 --> 00:01:29,959
Choose Save progress to
save the unfinished run.

28
00:01:30,289 --> 00:01:33,840
The sheet stays open, so choose
Close to return to the list

29
00:01:33,889 --> 00:01:35,340
and review the saved entry.

30
00:01:35,590 --> 00:01:37,809
Local drafts now shows Draft 1.

31
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:44,070
Choose History to load the saved run list,
then open the timestamped Engine 51 entry.

32
00:01:44,509 --> 00:01:47,549
The vehicle and time help you
find the work you just saved.

33
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:52,099
Save progress keeps the run available
for review before final submission.

34
00:01:52,450 --> 00:01:55,679
That matters during handover, when
someone needs to check the entered

35
00:01:55,679 --> 00:01:57,860
answers before finalizing the record.

36
00:01:58,070 --> 00:02:01,369
The reopened run brings back
the first item's Pass answer,

37
00:02:01,660 --> 00:02:03,539
equipment note and general note.

38
00:02:04,010 --> 00:02:07,859
Read them together and compare them with
the intended record before continuing.

39
00:02:08,329 --> 00:02:12,840
Save progress and Submit checklist remain
available while this is the working run.

40
00:02:13,329 --> 00:02:16,920
For a community care vehicle, this
review gives the next operator

41
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:21,420
the answer, its explanation and
the overall context in one place.

42
00:02:21,559 --> 00:02:24,879
When the review is complete,
choose Submit checklist.

43
00:02:25,289 --> 00:02:28,420
The sheet changes to Submitted, Score 100.

44
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:32,820
The answer fields are now read-only,
and Close remains available.

45
00:02:33,230 --> 00:02:35,809
Save progress and Submit
checklist are gone.

46
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:39,800
The score is the result of the
answers entered in this training form.

47
00:02:40,229 --> 00:02:43,679
Read the returned state to confirm
that the run has reached submission.

48
00:02:43,910 --> 00:02:47,820
After reopening the run from refreshed
History, the submitted result and

49
00:02:47,820 --> 00:02:49,479
training notes are still present.

50
00:02:49,850 --> 00:02:52,640
Check them before handing the
record to another operator.

51
00:02:53,090 --> 00:02:57,390
Carry the same target, answer,
note and review habit to a wildland

52
00:02:57,390 --> 00:03:00,979
vehicle or industrial support
equipment using the appropriate form.

53
00:03:01,460 --> 00:03:06,380
This example covers saving and reopening
in the same browser tab; offline use,

54
00:03:06,579 --> 00:03:10,469
browser restarts and device-location
behavior need separate checks.

